# Keep LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows checks text files out with CRLF while build.js
# writes LF, so `node build.js --check` reports all twelve outputs stale on a
# fresh clone and `node build.js` leaves the tree permanently dirty. The repo
# itself already stores LF; this only stops the checkout from rewriting it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched by line-ending conversion.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text eol=lf
